# Exact decimal addition of tenths and hundredths

Adds 0.1 and 0.2, then 0.01 and 0.02, to verify fractions that binary
floating-point cannot represent sum exactly in decimal, producing 0.3 and
0.03 instead of 0.30000000000000004 and 0.030000000000000002.

>>> source
tenths: decimal = 0.1 + 0.2
print(tenths)

hundredths: decimal = 0.01 + 0.02
print(hundredths)

<<< stdout
0.3
0.03

<<< stderr
